Q3. Difference between Observer Pattern
and Strategy Pattern

Interview Ready Answer

Observer Pattern

• Behavioral Design Pattern.
• One-to-Many Relationship.
• Subject notifies all registered
  observers.
• Focuses on Event Notification.
• Used when state changes
  need to be communicated.

Example

YouTube Channel

↓

Subscribers

↓

Notification

------------------------------------------------------------

Strategy Pattern

• Behavioral Design Pattern.
• Defines multiple algorithms
  for the same task.
• Client selects one strategy
  at runtime.
• Focuses on changing behavior.
• Removes tight coupling
  between algorithms.

Example

Payment

↓

UPI Strategy

Credit Card Strategy

Net Banking Strategy

------------------------------------------------------------

Memory Trick

Observer

↓

One Subject

↓

Many Observers

↓

